§8: every table layer reads the same head — `@@type[…]("…"){…}%%numberType` —
so a slot pair, the specs items and a numbering marker reach the `<table>`, the
`<caption>`, a column's `<th>`, the `<tbody>`, a `<tr>`, a `<td>` and the
`<tfoot>` alike. Nothing is layer-specific except *where* the head sits:

|-[tbl-slug]("Table title")@@tableX{.t}%%%numberA -|
||@@captionX[cap-slug]("Cap title"){.c}%%%numberA A caption ||
| A | B | C |
| :---@@thX[th-slug]("Th title"){.v}%%%numberA | ---: | --- |@@tbodyX{.tb}
|@@cellX[cl-slug]("Cl title"){.cl}%%%numberA 1 | 2 | 3 |@@rowX{.rw}
|===|@@tfootX[ft-slug]("Ft title"){.ft}%%%numberA
| Total | > | 9 |

The column extras above stay on the `<th>` (§8/OPEN-E1): the `<td>` under it
keeps only the alignment, which is why `cellX` appears once.
